[x] Make read charters --format json conform to charters.schema.json $specifications/schemas/charters.schema.json now exists. Replace semantic_charters_json (clearhead-cli/src/cli/charter.rs) with a core schema_export-style charter projection: single {charters:\[...]} document, lowercase state, no embedded actions/plans, omit nulls, split Log/sibling sections out of description, keep defaults. Ids follow clearhead-core docs/DECISIONS.md Decision 1. Then add the pinned-CLI projection check to scripts/validate-pinned step 3. RESOLVED 2026-09-23 in clearhead-core 085ebef and platform 71c4460. Core workspace/charter_schema.rs now projects a loaded MarkdownCharter and its document bytes into canonical schema facts: lowercase local state, single flat {charters:\[...]} across workspaces, no nested actions/plans/null fields, declared matching document id only (sidecar/shell ids omitted), source defaults, core description, Log entries and ordered sibling sections. CLI read charters JSON assembles before printing and errors if an existing source cannot be reread. scripts/validate-pinned step 3 validates the actual pinned CLI output against specifications/schemas/charters.schema.json, not just the example. Reviewer found and we fixed two rounds of BLOCK issues: unclosed/long Markdown fences lost content, fractional timestamps and whitespace-padded dates violated schema, and empty title/alias/parent/objectives could violate minLength/minItems. Regressions cover each, plus multi-workspace and filtered-empty output. Full core gate, real 26-charter schema validation, scripts/validate-pinned, and fresh different-model final review passed. Legacy heading-style Log content is preserved as undated text; its source migration remains action 01a0ccb0-82ab-74a9-8b9c-c75730082150.$ ^2026-09-22T17:40 %2026-09-23T10:16 #01a0cbb5-0604-7386-ba34-ded646e7f9d4
